Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS  
  – "Icd10Code": join to ICD10CODE to decide whether a record belongs to the “discharge” or “vehicle” group.  
  – "RaceRecode3": identify White decedents ("RaceRecode3" = 1 from RACERECODE3).  
  – "AgeRecode27", "AgeRecode12", "AgeRecode52": pre‑built age–group codes; any of them can be aggregated on.  
  – "Id": unique row identifier that can be counted when computing deaths.  

• DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE  
  – "Code": join key to DEATHRECORDS."Icd10Code".  
  – "Description": filter for text that ILIKE '%discharge%' (excluding the three unwanted phrases) or ILIKE '%vehicle%'.  

• DEATH.DEATH.RACERECODE3  
  – "Code" / "Description": lookup table that tells us White = 1.  

• DEATH.DEATH.AGERECODE27 (or AGERECODE12 / 52)  
  – "Code" / "Description": attaches readable age‑group names to the numeric code in DEATHRECORDS.  

The condition set we will need repeatedly  
1. White only → DR."RaceRecode3" = 1  
2. “Discharge” ICD set → IC."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%' AND  
   NOT IC."Description" ILIKE '%urethral discharge%' AND  
   NOT IC."Description" ILIKE '%discharge of firework%' AND  
   NOT IC."Description" ILIKE '%firearm discharge%'  
3. “Vehicle” ICD set → IC."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20) that progress from simple inspections to the final comparison.  
Every identifier is wrapped in double quotes and each query is preceded by a short comment.

```sql
-- 1. Look at a sample of ICD‑10 codes whose description contains the word “discharge”
SELECT DISTINCT
       IC."Code",
       IC."Description"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE AS IC
WHERE  IC."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Check ICD‑10 codes whose description contains the word “vehicle”
SELECT DISTINCT
       IC."Code",
       IC."Description"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE AS IC
WHERE  IC."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Verify which code in RACERECODE3 equals White
SELECT *
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.RACERECODE3
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect the predefined age‑group catalogue (27‑group version)
SELECT *
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.AGERECODE27
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count deaths of Whites whose ICD description meets the “discharge” rule (after exclusions) – raw counts
SELECT
       DR."Icd10Code",
       COUNT(*) AS "death_count"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS  AS DR
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE     AS IC
         ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1                             -- White
  AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
  AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
  AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
  AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%firearm discharge%'
GROUP  BY DR."Icd10Code"
ORDER  BY "death_count" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Count deaths of Whites with ICD descriptions that contain “vehicle” – raw counts
SELECT
       DR."Icd10Code",
       COUNT(*) AS "death_count"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS  AS DR
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE     AS IC
         ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1
  AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
GROUP  BY DR."Icd10Code"
ORDER  BY "death_count" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Average number of “discharge” deaths per ICD code within each 27‑group age band (Whites only)
SELECT
       DR."AgeRecode27"                       AS "age_code",
       AVG(cnt)                               AS "avg_discharge_deaths"
FROM (
        SELECT DR."AgeRecode27",
               DR."Icd10Code",
               COUNT(*) AS cnt
        FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS  AS DR
        JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE     AS IC
               ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
        WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1
          AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
          AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
          AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
          AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%firearm discharge%'
        GROUP  BY DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code"
      ) q
GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27"
ORDER BY DR."AgeRecode27"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Average number of “vehicle” deaths per ICD code within each 27‑group age band (Whites only)
SELECT
       DR."AgeRecode27"                       AS "age_code",
       AVG(cnt)                               AS "avg_vehicle_deaths"
FROM (
        SELECT DR."AgeRecode27",
               DR."Icd10Code",
               COUNT(*) AS cnt
        FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS  AS DR
        JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE     AS IC
               ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
        WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1
          AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
        GROUP  BY DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code"
      ) q
GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27"
ORDER BY DR."AgeRecode27"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Bring readable age‑group names together with both averages
WITH discharge_avg AS (
    SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", AVG(cnt) AS "avg_discharge"
    FROM (
          SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code", COUNT(*) AS cnt
          FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS AS DR
          JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    AS IC
                ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
          WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1
            AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
            AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
            AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
            AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%firearm discharge%'
          GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code"
         ) x
    GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27"
),
vehicle_avg AS (
    SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", AVG(cnt) AS "avg_vehicle"
    FROM (
          SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code", COUNT(*) AS cnt
          FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS AS DR
          JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    AS IC
                ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
          WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1
            AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
          GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code"
         ) y
    GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27"
)
SELECT
       AR."Description"               AS "age_group",
       d."avg_discharge",
       v."avg_vehicle"
FROM   discharge_avg AS d
JOIN   vehicle_avg   AS v
  ON   d."AgeRecode27" = v."AgeRecode27"
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.AGERECODE27 AS AR
  ON   AR."Code" = d."AgeRecode27"
ORDER  BY d."AgeRecode27"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final step: compute the difference (how much higher “discharge” average is than “vehicle” average) per age group
WITH discharge_avg AS (
    SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", AVG(cnt) AS "avg_discharge"
    FROM (
          SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code", COUNT(*) AS cnt
          FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS AS DR
          JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    AS IC
                ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
          WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1
            AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
            AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
            AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
            AND  IC."Description" NOT ILIKE '%firearm discharge%'
          GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code"
         ) x
    GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27"
),
vehicle_avg AS (
    SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", AVG(cnt) AS "avg_vehicle"
    FROM (
          SELECT DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code", COUNT(*) AS cnt
          FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS AS DR
          JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    AS IC
                ON DR."Icd10Code" = IC."Code"
          WHERE  DR."RaceRecode3" = 1
            AND  IC."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
          GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27", DR."Icd10Code"
         ) y
    GROUP BY DR."AgeRecode27"
)
SELECT
       AR."Description"                                  AS "age_group",
       d."avg_discharge",
       v."avg_vehicle",
       (d."avg_discharge" - v."avg_vehicle")             AS "avg_diff_discharge_minus_vehicle"
FROM   discharge_avg AS d
JOIN   vehicle_avg   AS v
  ON   d."AgeRecode27" = v."AgeRecode27"
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.AGERECODE27 AS AR
  ON   AR."Code" = d."AgeRecode27"
ORDER  BY d."AgeRecode27"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries move step‑by‑step from exploring the underlying dimensional tables to producing the requested comparison of average death counts for White individuals by age group.
