--Description:  The earlier error occurred because the outer query referenced the alias DR, which
--              exists only inside the sub‑query.  To fix this, the outer layer must reference the
--              derived‑table alias q when selecting and grouping by "AgeRecode27".
--              Logic:
--              1) Inner query → for White decedents (RaceRecode3 = 1), find every combination of
--                 AgeRecode27 and Icd10Code whose ICD description contains “discharge” but excludes
--                 “Urethral discharge”, “Discharge of firework”, and any “firearm discharge”.
--                 Count the deaths in each combination (cnt).
--              2) Outer query → average those counts across all ICD codes within each age band,
--                 giving the average number of “discharge” deaths per code for each AgeRecode27.
SELECT
       q."AgeRecode27"            AS "age_code",
       AVG(q.cnt)                 AS "avg_discharge_deaths"
FROM (
        SELECT
               DR."AgeRecode27",
               DR."Icd10Code",
               COUNT(*) AS cnt
        FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS AS DR
        JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    AS IC
